{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1795441680","published":"2026-11-23T13:48:37Z","modified":"2026-11-26T07:45:08.565607855Z","upstream":["CVE-2023-54207","CVE-2024-58002","CVE-2025-38007","CVE-2025-40154","CVE-2026-23392","CVE-2026-43363","CVE-2026-53253","CVE-2026-63905","CVE-2026-72339","CVE-2026-74488","CVE-2026-90204","CVE-2026-90205","CVE-2026-93826"],"summary":"Fix of 12 CVEs","details":"   * Bump kernel ABI to 36: ship the ELS kernel as 4.19.0-36-*, distinct from\n     the prior 4.19.0-35.\n   * CVE-2023-54207\n     - HID: uclogic: Correct devm device reference for hidinput input_dev\n       name {CVE-2023-54207}\n   * CVE-2024-58002\n     - media: uvcvideo: Only save async fh if success {CVE-2024-58002}\n     - media: uvcvideo: Remove redundant NULL assignment {CVE-2024-58002}\n     - media: uvcvideo: Remove dangling pointers {CVE-2024-58002}\n   * CVE-2025-38007\n     - HID: uclogic: Add NULL check in uclogic_input_configured()\n       {CVE-2025-38007}\n   * CVE-2025-40154\n     - ASoC: Intel: bytcr_rt5640: Fix invalid quirk input mapping\n       {CVE-2025-40154}\n   * CVE-2026-23392\n     - netfilter: nf_tables: release flowtable after rcu grace period on\n       error {CVE-2026-23392}\n   * CVE-2026-43363\n     - x86/apic: Disable x2apic on resume if the kernel expects so\n       {CVE-2026-43363}\n   * CVE-2026-53253\n     - skbuff: introduce skb_pull_data {CVE-2026-53253}\n     - Bluetooth: bnep: fix incorrect length parsing in bnep_rx_frame()\n       extension handling {CVE-2026-53253}\n     - Bluetooth: bnep: reject short frames before parsing\n       {CVE-2026-53253}\n   * CVE-2026-63905\n     - usbip: vudc: Fix use after free bug in vudc_remove due to race\n       condition {CVE-2026-63905}\n   * CVE-2026-72339\n     - qede: fix off-by-one in BD ring consumption on build_skb failure\n       {CVE-2026-72339}\n   * CVE-2026-74488\n     - wifi: mwifiex: use the subframe length when parsing A-MSDU TDLS\n       frames {CVE-2026-74488}\n   * CVE-2026-90204\n     - ocfs2: validate DIO orphan slot during inode read {CVE-2026-90204}\n   * CVE-2026-90205\n     - ocfs2: validate orphan slot during inode read {CVE-2026-90205}\n   * CVE-2026-93826\n     - hid: hid-logitech-hidpp: avoid unnecessary assignments in\n       hidpp_connect_event {CVE-2026-93826}\n     - HID: hidpp: fix potential UAF in hidpp_connect_event()\n       {CVE-2026-93826}\n   * Miscellaneous upstream changes\n     - sctp: hold transport reference across connect wait","affected":[{"package":{"name":"hyperv-daemons","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/hyperv-daemons?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-9+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1795441680.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libbpf-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libbpf-dev?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-9+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1795441680.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libbpf4.19","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libbpf4.19?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-9+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1795441680.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libcpupower-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libcpupower-dev?distro=debian-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.325-9+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian10els/CLSA-2026-1795441680.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libcpupower1","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:10","pu